25AV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24518, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Fc6fXCz5y6eRJ7iLAeyUGi", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after updating us-east, leaving regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, service healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the rollout orchestrator error, and check why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55118, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Fc6fXCz5y6eRJ7iLAeyUGi", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55118, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Fc6fXCz5y6eRJ7iLAeyUGi", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57032, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SMiwudqMniNTwjm4viAzV2", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57332, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SMiwudqMniNTwjm4viAzV2", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57332, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SMiwudqMniNTwjm4viAzV2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62160, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the failing release.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, so the regions were briefly on different versions. A second attempt finished the job.\n- us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service is healthy and the error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- No approval was needed: v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before, so the change-manager rule doesn't apply.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had gone through, so I didn't create a second one or page on-call twice.\n- The incident covers what happened, the rollback (including the failed first attempt) and the current state. It lists three follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed.\n  - Look into the orchestrator error.\n  - Find out how v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate had already failed in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BofHxmJ7FNfTf2QLy9vcVX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019Cz4ok1QjPeFsMqcMnWnvD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_017EZ24H8EUiEpGa1LS99Kxe"